From b22ad8968ae3ec17cd9a40e7acd5455a7203dc25 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Siddhartha Srivastava <siddhartha@delphai.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 15:43:28 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Rules 3: verified generation jobs (head stage, Gumbel-max
 sampling, generated tokens)

A generation batch is one sequence: its input row is the prompt then GenSentinel. Each batch
gets a head stage after its layer groups: per position HN (final norm), HQ (lm_head
quantization), per 1024-token vocabulary chunk HL (scores; an element needs one lm_head row)
and HC (the chunk's best), and HS (the sample: the stage's outputs). Greedy or Gumbel-max with
counter-based noise (splitmix64 over job id, position, token; detLog port). Stage 0 reads a
generated token from the head stage (RowGenToken against its opened root). The job's output
root commits the head output roots; a head stage opens only with its path in it (OutProof).
Generation models commit norm + lm_head in the weights tree. MODEL_REG / JOB_POST / reveal
encodings and job/model state gain suffixes only when set. Tests: bit-exact head stage, noise
and det_log vs runtime/bench/export_gen_fixture.py; games on a generation job (lying provider
slashed on a score, a chunk best, a sample, an inconsistent generated token; honest provider
wins; forged output-root path and prompt-token replacement rejected); wire format; Rules gate.

